{
  "requirement": "The method is declared under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.check_inputs`.\n\nThe method resolves the recorded dependencies through graph operations and\nfingerprinting, comparing each with its saved observation. A fingerprint\nmismatch returns `Ok(false)` and permits an early return; it need not resolve\nlater dependencies. An encountered dependency-resolution failure returns an\nerror.\n\nThe method observes the current state that the caller intends to inspect.\nFreshness checking has a separate observation scope from criterion execution.\nChecked observations enter the new trace when execution explicitly reads\nor delivers them.\nA checked snapshot can be reused if it still represents the current state.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged the tests against each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.checking_records`. I did not read implementation source. The assessment rests on the supplied test text.\n\n- **Resolve and compare each dependency, and return `Ok(false)` on a mismatch.**\n  - `a_matching_dependency_does_not_hide_a_later_changed_dependency` has a matching first dependency and a later changed `Dependency::Node` or `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`. It asserts that `is_current` turns false.\n  - `wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors` covers a changed content fingerprint and a different fingerprint scheme.\n  - `labeled_selections_track_only_target_membership_without_reading_contents` covers edge-membership change. It also shows unrelated label or edge changes leave the record current.\n  - `changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another`, `absence_certification_is_invalidated_by_the_first_selected_root` and `dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers` assert `check_inputs` returns `Ok(false)` or `Ok(true)` through the `Validator`.\n  - The early return on a mismatch is optional (\"permits\"), so it needs no test.\n- **Return an error on a dependency-resolution failure.**\n  - `dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers` injects read and edge failures. It asserts `Err(\"read\")` and `Err(\"edges\")` from `check_inputs`. It also asserts that nothing is executed or rewritten.\n  - `wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors` and `labeled_selections_track_only_target_membership_without_reading_contents` assert errors from `is_current`.\n  - `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence` shows loading does not resolve inputs.\n- **Observe the current state the caller intends to inspect.**\n  - `requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk` builds a fresh domain after the files change. It asserts the old record is no longer current, while the retained snapshot's fingerprint is unchanged.\n  - `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` changes content after saving and asserts `check_inputs` sees the change.\n  - `refresh_evaluates_missing_incompatible_or_changed_evidence_with_a_fresh_trace` covers the same for content and successor changes.\n- **Freshness checking has a separate observation scope from execution, and checked observations enter the new trace only on an explicit read or delivery.**\n  - `historical_freshness_reads_do_not_enter_the_replacement_trace` asserts that the read of node 2 during the check is not in the replacement record. Only the explicit root read of node 1 is.\n  - `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` asserts the new record holds only the explicitly read node, with its current \"after\" content.\n  - `refresh_evaluates_missing_incompatible_or_changed_evidence_with_a_fresh_trace` asserts reads `[2,1]` but dependencies containing only node 1.\n  - `source_reads_track_optional_dependencies_and_empty_searches_remain_discovery` covers delivered reads and discovery.\n- **A checked snapshot can be reused while it still represents the current state.** This is permissive wording, so it needs no test. The retained-snapshot fingerprint assertions in `requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk` cover it anyway.\n\nI found no unasserted obligation and no marking gap.",
